<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chikhori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1463</span> · Also known as Battle of Chikhori (1463)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chikhori was fought in 1463 in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, where Bagrat, a prince who had made himself king of Imereti, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-viii-of-georgia">George VIII of Georgia</a> with the help of the atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a>. The victory confirmed the break-up of the united Georgian kingdom into the separate realms of Imereti, Kartli, Kakheti and Samtskhe.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-chikhori.jpg" alt="Battle of Chikhori" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Caucasus topographic map-fr.svg by Bourrichon - fr:Bourrichon This derivative by Don-kun and WajWohu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caucasus_1450_map_de.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
